2. Fetch the trunk and rebase onto it:
   `git -C {{ shell_quote(worktree_path) }} fetch origin {{ shell_quote(trunk) }}`
   `git -C {{ shell_quote(worktree_path) }} rebase {{ shell_quote("origin/" ~ trunk) }}`
3. Resolve any conflicts yourself. Read both sides of each conflict and keep the
   intent of both. For `uv.lock`, take the trunk version and run `uv sync`. Use
   `GIT_EDITOR=true` with `git rebase --continue`, and `git rebase --skip` when a
   commit becomes empty.
4. If no commits remain after the rebase, they were already on the trunk: report
   `subsumed` and stop.
5. Push with
   `git -C {{ shell_quote(worktree_path) }} push --force-with-lease --force-if-includes origin {{ shell_quote(branch) }}`.
6. Remove the worktree you created with `git worktree remove` (no `--force`). Do
   not delete branches or worktrees you did not create.

